hey everyone this is Alessandra and I'm  here to talk about metal wolf chaos XD  the remaster for From Software's cult  hit from the original Xbox  before the days of the stoic Dark Souls  from software was a niche developer  nestled between releases of the mecha  action series ARMA core and the  occasional oddball side project 15 years  ago they released a game that blended  these two talents together in the form  of metal wolf chaos in the years since  it has lived something of a second life  as an internet meme so it's been  especially strange to see it return for  a third with a remaster so with that I  want to take a quick look back on the  history of metal wolf chaos and talk  about why it's so bizarre and somewhat  eerie to see it back to the White House  putting you in the role the 47th  President of the United States Michael  Wilson you battled legions of soldiers  and machines of war across America  following a coup led by Vice President  Richard hawk  essentially metal wolf chaos is this  weird pastiche of American action films  and Japanese mecha anime playing through  this strange satire of American culture  today can be a fun trip down memory lane  circa 2004 developed on a budget and in  under a year by 30 developers metal wolf  chaos keeps things simple leaning  heavily on the over-the-top mecha action  with this revolving set of weaponry it's  a setup that seemed like it would have  made for a decent action game for the  North American audience however it would  never arrive in the West the original  metal wolf chaos for the Xbox was a  japan-only release positioned as a game  intended to attract new players to the  system unfortunately it wouldn't make  much of a dent in the market and its  release came and went at the time  publishers were already transitioning to  the upcoming Xbox 360 and the games  satire of terrorism and American culture  likely made it a tough sell playing  through the game now it's hard not to  draw parallels with the events and  storytelling tropes of the game with  today's political climate with homegrown  terrorism fascism and propaganda on the  rise in the u.s. it can make some of the  events of the game feel eerie even when  its story is totally absurd metal wolf  chaos is a political game even when it  focuses on dumb fun action its original  release came during the height of Bush  era jingoism and the bizarre story and  characters reflect that to play a metal  wolf chaos is to contend with a barrage  of one-liners melodrama and cheesy  platitudes of what it means to be an  American and it does everything with the  utmost sincerity it's essentially a  Japanese anime honed through an American  fetishize lens crafted by Michael Bay  though the u.s. missed out on the full  game some Western players have the  chance to try a small slice of the game  thanks to demo discs from the official  Xbox Magazine one in particular featured  a hidden demo for metal wolf chaos  allowing players to jump into the game's  early levels set in San Francisco unless  you own an imported Japanese Xbox or  modified your system to play games  region-free this will be the only way  for Western players to experience the  game but in 2016  indie publisher devolver digital whose  past works include hotline Miami and The  Shadow Warrior reboot reach  after fromsoftware on twitter offering  to get the game released in the West  after the tweet went viral devolver  digital and from software began their  collaboration or to remaster for modern  consoles when compared to the original  metal wolf chaos xt keeps things  faithful low poly count in all some  notable changes however include the  upgraded resolution to play at 4k and a  new safe system that feels a bit more up  at the times in a way though the low  budget offers an aesthetic that adds  charm to the ridiculous plot and  straightforward gameplay in that regard  it fills that similar so bizarre it's  good space that games like deadly  permission inhabited  metal wolf chaos never lets up with its  headfirst approach to satirizing  American action films and culture in  many ways the tone and plot of this cult  hit lands harder now than ever before  likely more than the creator's ever  imagined  [Music]  you
 

